Major updates will go here probably

Several first milestones
First upload includes a couple weeks worth of progress, my major milestones roughly in order up until now are:
- Main menu with start settings and info pages
- Start sends to landing page with starting dialogue, options, and a character card
- Used the starting out card to creat all following info/dialogue cards
- Character card includes health bar, progress bar, a map section (possible feature later), gold, and an inventory
- Formatted the page to be easy to look at and work with
- Added a few intro choices to get used to the process of moving between info cards (areas)
- Added functionality to add and subtract health from the health bar
- Added a store that checks your gold and allows you to add items to your inventory - SWORD, ARMOR, and POTION
- Prevented purchase of multiples of a single item
- Created custom JSON data for the intro sequence including multiple paths to the 'HUB' area
- Created 3 directional choices for player to choose from
- Added a simple JSON-based scenario to set up combat encounter in the WEST tree
- Added an enemy with same health bar functionality, formatted to the right side of the screen - OGRE
- Added 2 combat options of ATTACK and USE POTION - may chance this functionality in the future
- ATTACK option deals variable damage with a chance to deal critical damage, variable damage is returned at the same time
- ATTACK option deals flat higher damage if a SWORDis equipped
- OGRE deals less damage if you are wearing ARMOR
- USE POTION checks for a potion in inventory and heals the user for a flat amount if they have one
- Added a random loot table to the OGRE upon death, user can receive one of 3 items based on chance
- Added selling functionality to the shop
- Blocked the user form re-entering an area they have already cleared
- Added death
- Added ability to use a potion anywhere straight from inventory, opening up the possibility for a change in the combat system

2nd major push: - this push didn't get pushed real cool
Added most of the leadup scenario for killing the crabs
- Dialogue, options
- Dialogue tree that goes to the fight, will fill in rest later
- Added functionality for attacking crab 1, and all 3 returning damage

3rd major puch:
Fleshed out the crab code, copied versions of it for attacking crabs 2 and 3
- cleaned up console logs and unreached code
- Copied code for all 3 crabs, making relevant changes for each one
- Ensured combat could be approached in any order
- First draft of changes to loot system from crabs, might refine

4th major push:
Cleaned up east encounter, steamlined some code, added all dialogue options for East section:
- Allowed the encounter to end after killing all crabs - looked for a way to do it with 1 less input, will clean this up if I have time doesnt affect the game overall tho
- Tied up all the dialogue trees, added a couple other routes to crab encounter and a couple ways to the knight encounter and a route to retire
- Added knight encounter - in it's current state it is there to be impossible the knight basically always kills you this is intentional!
- Upon finishing crab encounter, you now get the completed popup, loot dialogue (actual loot not yet added) and a return to town button 
- added a check for if the player has completed both the east and west sections so they can now enter the north (WIP)

5th major push:
Added final area and dragon fight, as well as cleaned up a lot of wonky stuff:
- North area now works once the player has beaten the east and west sections
- North features a dragon fight with a bunch of other "adventurers"
- Added all dialogue and options for the North section
- Finishing the fight ends the game and posts the data including a final score
- Fleshed out the return button functionality
- Added font changing and info box
- Cleaned up a bunch of code, added comments where needed and clarification on why I made choices
- Death and retirement both now restart the game properly (wanted to do a more elaborate death sequence but time was a factor for it)

Final push before hand in:
- Got a playtest, fixed some bugs, some remain I'm sure
- Final checks for anything terrible, all seems to be ok
